        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          Paddle weight is the spec players argue about most and understand least. The number on the listing is only part of the story: where that weight sits in the paddle changes how it swings, and the right weight for you depends on your strength, your arm history and whether you win points by driving or by dinking. Get it right and the paddle disappears in your hand. Get it wrong and you will feel it in your elbow by the end of the week.
        </p>

        <TopPick />

        <div id="bands" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. The Three Weight Bands
          </h2>

          <p>
            Manufacturers and retailers broadly sort paddles into three weight bands. Lightweight paddles weigh about 7.5 ounces or less, midweight paddles run from roughly 7.6 to 8.2 ounces, and heavyweight paddles start at about 8.3 ounces. These are common industry conventions rather than official categories, and individual brands sometimes draw the lines a tenth of an ounce higher or lower, but they are the language you will see on almost every listing.
          </p>

          <p>
            Most paddles are listed with a weight range rather than a single number, such as 7.8 to 8.2 ounces, because the materials used in face sheets, cores and edge guards vary slightly from one paddle to the next. If the exact weight matters to you, weigh the paddle yourself on a kitchen scale when it arrives. A difference of a quarter of an ounce is noticeable to many players, especially at the kitchen line, where the paddle is moved quickly over short distances.
          </p>

          <p>
            Remember too that grips and edge guards add weight. An overgrip adds a small amount, and lead tape, covered below, adds whatever you choose. The weight printed on the listing is the starting point, not necessarily what you will play with after customisation.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
